Alchemy could be a skill. An alchemist class would be able to reach
expert. Wizards, priests, healers, and rogues would be able to reach
basic, and all other classes would be restricted - rogues because they
brew up poisons and blackmarket booze.

At basic skill, alchemy would work as it does now. At unskilled,
it would be worse - 20% chance of explosion, unable to make full
healing, etc. At skilled or expert, the chance of explosion would
fall, and more potions would become available

E.g, at skilled you might be able to make a potion of strong acid,
with double the normal effect, by dipping booze into acid, while
at expert you might be able to make potions of controlled polymorph
from gain level and polymorph.

Stronger versions of several existing potions would work -
strong booze, madness instead of hallucination, flight instead
of levitation - and some new ones could be added for experts:
clairvoyance, gold detection, fear.


